[{ "action": "append", "id": "event-modals", "value" : "<div tabindex=\"-1\" id=\"modal-0d37006b-8fb8-42ca-989f-cee9ff082c8d\" class=\"modal\"><div class=\"modal-dialog modal-lg\"><div class=\"modal-content\"><div class=\"modal-header\"><a data-dismiss=\"modal\" class=\"close\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-remove\"></span></a><p class=\"text-muted\"><span class=\"glyphicon glyphicon-road\"></span> Research papers</p><strong>Fri 9 Oct 2026 10:30 - 10:48 at <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/room/issta-2026/splash-issta-2026-venue-east-hall-1\" class=\"room-link navigate\">East Hall 1</a></strong> - <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/track/issta-2026/issta-2026-research-papers#program\" class=\"navigate\">Fuzzing and Exploit Generation</a> <small>Chair(s): <a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/liliwei1\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\">Lili Wei</a></small></div><div class=\"modal-body\"><div class=\"bg-primary event-title\"><h4><span data-event-star=\"0d37006b-8fb8-42ca-989f-cee9ff082c8d\" title=\"Add event to your program\"><span class=\"text-disabled glyphicon glyphicon-star-empty\"></span></span><strong>PoCE: Automated Proof-of-Concept Synthesis using Large Language Models for Robust Validation</strong></h4></div><div class=\"bg-info event-description\"><p>Vulnerability reports play a critical role in software repair, with Proof-of-Concept (PoC) exploits serving as one of their most essential components. PoC exploits enable software developers to reliably reproduce reported vulnerabilities and subsequently deploy patches. However, generating effective PoCs is costly, expertise-intensive, and increasingly challenging due to the diversity of modern software ecosystems and their complex dependencies. Inadequate or incorrect PoCs can significantly delay patch deployment, thereby increasing the window of exposure to attacks. Prior work on automated PoC generation struggles to produce comprehensive and reliable exploits. In this work, we present an automated PoC generation framework, PoCE, capable of generating PoCs across diverse software systems by handling varied input formats and complex execution contexts using large language models. PoCE integrates structured in-context learning, retrieval-augmented generation, and iterative chain-of-thought reasoning to expand an initial exploitable PoC into multiple validated variants. These variants are executed in controlled environments to confirm exploitability. We evaluate PoCE on eleven widely used software projects, including TensorFlow, Yasm, Zlib, Liblouis, Cflow, TCPDUMP, Fig2dev, Binutils, libsndfile, LibTIFF, and libsixel. Our approach achieves an exploitation success rate of 78.1% and generates multiple exploit variants for most vulnerable cases, uncovering alternative exploit paths and edge conditions. We discover 57 zero-day PoCs and identify 26 previously unknown zero-day vulnerabilities in cross-layer software.</p>\n<p></p><p></p><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/tanusreedastithy\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Tanusree Das <span class=\"name-visual-sep\"></span>Tithy<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">The University of Texas at Arlington</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/lamiahasanrodoshi\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Lamia Hasan <span class=\"name-visual-sep\"></span>Rodoshi<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">The University of Texas at Arlington</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/aymanrafidazahar\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Ayman Rafid <span class=\"name-visual-sep\"></span>Azahar<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">The University of Texas at Arlington</span></h5></div></div></a></div><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/amlanabhidarshi\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Amlan Abhidarshi<span class=\"pull-right\"><small></small></span></h5><h5 class=\"media-heading\"><span class=\"text-black\">The University of Texas at Austin</span></h5></div></div></a></div></div><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-sm-6\"><a href=\"https://conf.researchr.org/profile/issta-2026/tabassumfaruk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"navigate\"><div class=\"media\"><span class=\"pull-left\"><img alt=\"micro-avatar\" src=\"https://conf.researchr.org/getDefaultImage/micro-avatar?1783985080000\" class=\"outputimage media-object thumbnail no-bottom-margin\"/></span><div class=\"media-body\"><h5 class=\"media-heading\">Tabassum F